{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules","id":826965,"title":"Urhan Ability with New Chase Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-09T11:33:58-08:00","id":826965,"title":"Urhan Ability with New Chase Rules","content":"So in the old days when a Chase was merely an extended, contested series of Stamina + Athletics rolls, Chase Down let Uratha in Urhan use Speed as their dice pool instead. Fantastic, gives them quite a significant boost.<br /> <br /> Last weekend, we ran a chase scene using the new Chase rules, and my Urhan player felt that it was unsatisfactory that he got to use Speed instead, claiming that it negatively impacted the point of having the Edge in a chase. He suggested changing the rule such that the Urhan character either gets a bonus to the rolls, but still have to use the pairing determined by the participant with the Edge, or they decrease the successes necessary in a chase.<br /> <br /> Has anybody else run into this yet, and how do you feel about my player's idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:44:57-08:00","id":826971,"title":"","content":"I asked something similar a while back, and one thing that was suggested was that speed <i>only </i>replaces stamina + athletics. In other words, the urhan player needs to get the edge to use the ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:12:51-08:00","id":826986,"title":"","content":"Or maybe that Urhan can choose each time - <b>He can use normal Chase Dicepool or use Speed as one, always.</b> Basically, that Urhan have always an Edge in his rolls and can dictate his Dicepool for the turn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:13:01-08:00","id":826987,"title":"","content":"Yeah. If you're modeling a boxing match with chase rules, it makes no sense for speed to replace, say, brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:14:12-08:00","id":826990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=826987#post826987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. If you're modeling a boxing match with chase rules, it makes no sense for speed to replace, say, brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask how Urhan Form can be used to model boxing match... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:17:16-08:00","id":826992,"title":"","content":"They don't even have hands...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:24:02-08:00","id":826994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=826992#post826992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't even have hands...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you use Quicksilver Flesh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:18:57-08:00","id":827025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=826971#post826971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked something similar a while back, and one thing that was suggested was that speed <i>only </i>replaces stamina + athletics. In other words, the urhan player needs to get the edge to use the ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's consistent with the wording of the ability:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a foot chase, an Urhan uses Speed in place of Stamina + Athletics. </div> </div> </div>That tells me that two things need to be true for the character to use this ability. The chase has to be a foot chase (as opposed to a social chase, or a car chase, or what have you), and the roll has to be Stamina + Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T13:49:09-08:00","id":827064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827025#post827025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That tells me that two things need to be true for the character to use this ability. The chase has to be a foot chase (as opposed to a social chase, or a car chase, or what have you), and the roll has to be Stamina + Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this.<br /> <br /> The Urhan in question should strive to get edge as often as possible. When she has edge, she can select &quot;Stamina + Athletics&quot; as the roll and then invoke the Urhan substitution rule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T02:44:00-08:00","id":827367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827025#post827025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's consistent with the wording of the ability:<br /> <br /> That tells me that two things need to be true for the character to use this ability. The chase has to be a foot chase (as opposed to a social chase, or a car chase, or what have you), and the roll has to be Stamina + Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is: ALL foot chases used to be only Stamina + Athletics. With the new chase rules, a physical foot chase can be a whole bewildering (and amazing!) world of checks.<br /> <br /> Here's my proposed solution after reading over ideas here:<br /> <br /> &quot;During a foot chase, <i>urhan</i> add their species factor to their Athletics skill.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, if the physical competence of pure movement comes into play, the urhan dominates (+3 dice), but if the roll is Wits + Streetwise to move quickly through a dangerous neighborhood, the urhan doesn't have any inherent bonus.<br /> <br /> Alternately, because urhan used to be incredible at every single foot chase, you can argue that they should get some bonus (+3 or +5) to ANY check made during a chase, because movement is inherently involved. Although, fast-talking your way into a club to escape would clearly violate this! :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","user":"FlailBot","date":". 02-10-2016, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T03:56:00-08:00","id":827393,"title":"","content":"Yeah, before urhan had an advantage in any chase. Now they only get an advantage <i>when it makes sense.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:19:33-08:00","id":827428,"title":"","content":"No, you do not understand - Urhan should <i>clearly</i> win boxing matches and master chiefs competitions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to proper running this - <b>I just let Urhan character with Edge to choose his Speed Dicepool. </b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If he is great urban runner ( high Wits+Streetwise ) he can use other dicepool. If not - his Urhan &quot;super chase&quot; one is still players option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-10-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:37:01-08:00","id":827469,"title":"","content":"Personally, it sounds more like your player just isn't a fan of the new system. I mean, he's already getting amazing bonuses from having a high speed, smaller body, and likely better initiative, and all that is before rolling before the first time. Werewolves are also remarkably adapt at knowing the territory they hunt in. You are also getting Size + Strength (base) + Dexterity (base) + 5 for the dice roll - that's far higher than almost any dice pool even other supernatural can come up with, even if the opponent has the Edge, even you take the cumulative -1 penalty. <br /> <br /> Chances are, the wolf is going to win. Remember, the basic number of successes is 5, before any modifiers (which tend to favor the werewolf). You should have a Speed of 14 in Urhan at minimum, and with the -1 penalty, should averages out to at least 4 successes. One roll, no matter who you are chasing, should hit the TN on average. Two at the most with more difficult chases or bad luck. Even with magical powers for an opponent to boost their Speed to 10 times the werewolf's Speed? That's still two rolls on average with some willpower. And that's a pretty powerful opponent if they can do that.<br /> <br /> And that's with just 2 in each Strength and Dexterity scores. The bare minimum. If you have higher than normal physical Attributes, or further boosts to your Speed from Fleet of Foot, Tactical Shifting 1 or Strength (Glory) Gift, then that just makes things even more lopsided. Hells, Predator's Unmatched Pursuit lets you double your Speed for 1 essence for a turn - that's 30+ dice you're rolling.<br /> <br /> Maybe your player feels compelled to use whatever dice pool that the Edge determines instead of using the superior Speed as a dice pool? Maybe he doesn't like the feeling of penalties stacking up? Maybe the player likes the idea of swapping around dice pools. I don't know. Yeah, letting the werewolf use Speed as a dice pool does negatively impact the point of having Edge - the Urhan is ALWAYS going to pick to use their Speed as a dice pool. Its effectively a +10 dice bonus before any penalties, which is just too huge to pass up. So, really, the Edge is pretty meaningless here, unless we're talking some spirit or supernatural with insanely huge speed and intiative scores with a head start. But it is still majorly in the werewolf's favor.<br /> <br /> So, in light of the above analysis, can I ask what exactly your player was dissatisfied with? Any of the proposed changes would make the Urhan less effective, which leads me to think there's either 1) a perception issue or 2) a dislike of using a single dice pool when everyone else gets to mix it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:37:55-08:00","id":827470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827428#post827428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to proper running this - <b>I just let Urhan character with Edge to choose his Speed Dicepool. </b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If he is great urban runner ( high Wits+Streetwise ) he can use other dicepool. If not - his Urhan &quot;super chase&quot; one is still players option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is almost literally no scenario where a player's Wits + Streetwise will be anywhere near as high as his Urhan Chase Down roll. Not until a really high Primal Urge, anyway.<br /> <br /> Your minimum speed in Urhan is like, 12. I guess maybe there is a scenario wherein one's Chase Down roll isn't his best choice based on some other weakness his quarry has, but those are pretty rare.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:45:45-08:00","id":827476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827469#post827469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in light of the above analysis, can I ask what exactly your player was dissatisfied with? Any of the proposed changes would make the Urhan less effective, which leads me to think there's either 1) a perception issue or 2) a dislike of using a single dice pool when everyone else gets to mix it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>My player is FlailBot, who posted upthread, but I <i>believe</i> it's 2).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think I'm fine leaving it as &quot;If the pool is Stamina + Athletics, the urhan gets to use Speed instead.&quot; I mean, they're not always going to be able to use the urhan form.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that it's not just a cumulative -1 penalty to not use the Edge's dice pool: they also lose 10-again. Still, 14 dice sans 10-again versus 6 dice with 10-again is an advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:47:26-08:00","id":827477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827470#post827470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is almost literally no scenario where a player's Wits + Streetwise will be anywhere near as high as his Urhan Chase Down roll. Not until a really high Primal Urge, anyway.<br /> <br /> Your minimum speed in Urhan is like, 12. I guess maybe there is a scenario wherein one's Chase Down roll isn't his best choice based on some other weakness his quarry has, but those are pretty rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it works as designed, even with new Chase rules - Urhan Form is super fast and almost sure to get to your Prey. And then you go in to Urshul... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T07:09:17-08:00","id":827486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827367#post827367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;During a foot chase, <i>urhan</i> add their species factor to their Athletics skill.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, if the physical competence of pure movement comes into play, the urhan dominates (+3 dice), but if the roll is Wits + Streetwise to move quickly through a dangerous neighborhood, the urhan doesn't have any inherent bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nitpick - the Urhan's species factor is 8, three higher than the average adult human (5). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827476#post827476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My player is FlailBot, who posted upthread, but I <i>believe</i> it's 2).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think I'm fine leaving it as &quot;If the pool is Stamina + Athletics, the urhan gets to use Speed instead.&quot; I mean, they're not always going to be able to use the urhan form.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, if its in the case of 2, I suggest simply striking the Urhan gets Speed, and give them the bonus for Initiative instead. Chase Down lets a werewolf pre-empt another character. So, using Chase Down, you automatically increase the bonus from higher initiative by 1 (Clash of Wills applies). If you don't have the higher Initiative, gain it. If you have the higher, you're considered to be double and take a -2 to the TN. And so on. <br /> <br /> In some cases, you might apply the werewolf's perception bonus as well, since you don't have to worry about guessing what direction someone turned if a path split.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, remember that it's not just a cumulative -1 penalty to not use the Edge's dice pool: they also lose 10-again. Still, 14 dice sans 10-again versus 6 dice with 10-again is an advantage. </div> </div> </div> True, but I honestly consider the 10-again to be negligable in most cases. Its exciting when it goes off, and fun for the game overall, but doesn't have nearly the impact that a -1 die penalty has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:58:19-08:00","id":827590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827367#post827367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is: ALL foot chases used to be only Stamina + Athletics. With the new chase rules, a physical foot chase can be a whole bewildering (and amazing!) world of checks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and if you were chasing your prey in some other way (say, for example, Wits + Streetwise to navigate through a crowded street) you wouldn't have been able to use that ability. The same is still true. Urhan is really good at running fast. If you're chasing someone in a context where running fast doesn't help, you can't use the ability. If you get the Edge, you can make sure the chase is about running fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:41:52-08:00","id":830638,"title":"","content":"There are new chase rules? Would someone be so kind as to tell me what book they're in? I just had the damndest time failing to find them in either the GMC or Werewolf 2.0, and I feel like I'm missing something right under my nose &gt;:T","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:47:01-08:00","id":830641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=830638#post830638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are new chase rules? Would someone be so kind as to tell me what book they're in? I just had the damndest time failing to find them in either the GMC or Werewolf 2.0, and I feel like I'm missing something right under my nose &gt;:T</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the new Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook. Other new features include more detailed vehicle rules, a Crafting Equipment system, and a system for building custom monsters called Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T18:09:55-08:00","id":830655,"title":"","content":"Thanks Charlaquin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T01:20:43-08:00","id":833109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827486#post827486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nitpick - the Urhan's species factor is 8, three higher than the average adult human (5).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the human doesn't get the species factor, so I went with the difference. It'd be a house-rule anyway, so the details are largely irrelevant until a satisfactory concept has been settled on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=827486#post827486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, if its in the case of 2, I suggest simply striking the Urhan gets Speed, and give them the bonus for Initiative instead. Chase Down lets a werewolf pre-empt another character. So, using Chase Down, you automatically increase the bonus from higher initiative by 1 (Clash of Wills applies). If you don't have the higher Initiative, gain it. If you have the higher, you're considered to be double and take a -2 to the TN. And so on.<br /> <br /> In some cases, you might apply the werewolf's perception bonus as well, since you don't have to worry about guessing what direction someone turned if a path split.</div> </div> </div> </div>To specify my discontent: we did a chase (me <i>urhan, </i>escaping two raging <i>gauru </i>teammates), in which I had Edge. I choose a dicepool my opponents would suck at (Wits + Survival, I think) and used my Speed as my dice pool. I handily won in the first round with 8 successes.<br /> <br /> What I felt didn't jive was mostly that the Chase Down <i>urhan</i> ability rules were written for a previous version of the Chase. They should be updated or clarified, imo, and that's what this thread is about. You make some good points about the stat changes of <i>urhan</i> already giving them an advantage. In a foot chase, for example, smaller size, +2 Dex (converts to higher Initiative), convert to less successes needed. That makes me think that it's a good idea to tone down the Chase Down ability.<br /> <br /> As per my previous suggestions, either:<br /> bonuses to Athletics<br /> bonuses to checks deemed by the DM to be &quot;primarily movement focused&quot;<br /> bonuses to all checks in a foot chase (not very elegant)<br /> <br /> <br /> What else...?<br /> Using Speed as a pool in place of Str+Athletics seems silly to me, because, as you pointed out, there is nary a situation where taking 14+ dice with a cumulative penalty is worse than taking ~4-6 dice. Most chases wouldn't last long enough for that to be relevant. Meaning the <i>urhan</i> takes Speed as his pool every single time, unless the GM specifically forbids it.<br /> <br /> What I like about &quot;bonuses to checks deemed by the DM to be 'primarily movement focused'&quot; is that a clever chaser could put an <i>urhan</i> into situations where its speed, size, and agility weren't relevant, thus taking away the bonus and possibly catching the fleeing wolf. To me, that sounds like a good interpretation of the new Chase rules. They're intended to give variety to Chases and allow players to creatively interpret chasing, using their strengths to overcome a phyiscally superior enemy (or to be given the slip by a fast-talking, slow-moving, smooth operator when they're the physically superior ones!). I think giving <i>urhan</i> a bonus to &quot;movement-based checks in a foot chase&quot; is an excellent compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","user":"FlailBot","date":". 02-19-2016, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T05:05:53-08:00","id":833167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=833109#post833109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but the human doesn't get the species factor, so I went with the difference. It'd be a house-rule anyway, so the details are largely irrelevant until a satisfactory concept has been settled on.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humans have a species factor equal to their Size. Wolves have a flat number, irregardless of Size. But, like you said, details are highly irrelevant, which is why I said it was nitpicking. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To specify my discontent: we did a chase (me <i>urhan, </i>escaping two raging <i>gauru </i>teammates), in which I had Edge. I choose a dicepool my opponents would suck at (Wits + Survival, I think) and used my Speed as my dice pool. I handily won in the first round with 8 successes.<br /> <br /> What I felt didn't jive was mostly that the Chase Down <i>urhan</i> ability rules were written for a previous version of the Chase. They should be updated or clarified, imo, and that's what this thread is about. You make some good points about the stat changes of <i>urhan</i> already giving them an advantage. In a foot chase, for example, smaller size, +2 Dex (converts to higher Initiative), convert to less successes needed. That makes me think that it's a good idea to tone down the Chase Down ability. </div> </div> </div> I don't understand the problem here. You used a form built for running to... flee from two forms not built for running? Do you not want Urhan to be the better at running? War form isnt' meant to be a quick-running form. Every form was designed with having a specific function in the hunt. <br /> <br /> Even if you use the old Chase rules, even if you use a lesser bonus, Urhan would still have handily won the chase. That's just how things are set up, irregardless of which rules you use, what bonus you change it to. Urhan is going to be awesome at outrunning anyone. <br /> <br /> And, while Chase Down was designed with old rules in mind... I seem to recall one David Hill, one of the Onyx Path writers, making a comment that the new Chase rules were designed with Werewolf specifically in mind, which makes me think that Urhan is working as intended under the new system. I could be misremembering, but I'm pretty confident. Given the &quot;inability to tire&quot; is also a consideration on the new Chase rules, I suspect that we're dealing <br /> <br /> It honestly sounds like its specifically Urhan's ability to be awesome at running that's the problem here. If you remove their bonus, you're negating a big part of their purpose in the Hunt. So, that's something to keep in mind. While here, specifically, you outran the Gauru, you need to keep in mind that Urhan will need the ability to chase down spirits and Claimed that are going to be good at running as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As per my previous suggestions, either:<br /> bonuses to Athletics<br /> bonuses to checks deemed by the DM to be &quot;primarily movement focused&quot;<br /> bonuses to all checks in a foot chase (not very elegant) </div> </div> </div> How about just +Primary Renown to any rolls that involve running? Its simple, and you seem to want a small bonus here to give other forms a chance on chasing down Urhan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T06:18:12-08:00","id":833203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/826965-urhan-ability-with-new-chase-rules?p=833167#post833167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Humans have a species factor equal to their Size.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the human species factor has gone back to just being 5 now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}